    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d377">

                <pb facs="0562" n="492" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv01/pg492"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72/12570a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Morris</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1918-12-19T16:00:00-05:00"
                            >December 19, 1918—4 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Press reports give summary of recent statement alleged to have been made by
                    Okuma, indicating Japan’s ambitions in South Sea Islands. Please cable substance
                    of statement, indicating reason for <pb facs="0563" n="493" xml:id="pg493"/>
                    statement, date, occasion upon which made, and such other information as you may
                    be able to obtain. Please mail full text in first pouch.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
